From: FlipperOneEmu
Subject: [PATCH] accel/tcg, target/arm: exceptions and interrupts without the BQL

cpu_exec took the BQL for each exception a vCPU took (a system call, a
page's abort) to call do_interrupt, and for each interrupt to ask the
target whether it takes it. Then, since Arm's do_interrupt sets EXITTB
after either, it took the BQL again at the next check to clear that bit.
With Flipper OS booting on eight cores, the vCPUs waited for the BQL
there in a third of their busy time, about as much at each of the two.

A target may now say that it takes an exception without the BQL
(do_interrupt_unlocked), or an interrupt (cpu_exec_interrupt_unlocked):
from the CPU's own state alone, a change of that state alone. cpu_exec
then calls do_interrupt or cpu_exec_interrupt without it. EXITTB alone
is cleared without it too: cpu_reset_interrupt is atomic. None of this
in record or replay, nor while single-stepping, nor for DEBUG, HALT or
RESET.

Arm's A profile says so on a CPU without a GICv3 CPU interface (whose
registers are the GIC's) while the EL change hooks have nothing to do
(patch 0013's test): for UDEF, SVC, prefetch and data aborts, IRQ and
FIQ, and for a physical IRQ or FIQ alone. PSCI's HVC and SMC,
semihosting and debug keep the BQL, and so does the M profile (its
NVIC).

---
--- a/include/accel/tcg/cpu-ops.h	2026-11-27 18:51:17.023581224 -0500
+++ b/include/accel/tcg/cpu-ops.h	2026-11-27 18:51:55.934260761 -0500
@@ -171,6 +171,12 @@
 #else
     /** @do_interrupt: Callback for interrupt handling.  */
     void (*do_interrupt)(CPUState *cpu);
+    /**
+     * @do_interrupt_unlocked: (optional) true if @do_interrupt may take
+     * cpu->exception_index's exception without the BQL: a change of the
+     * CPU's own state alone. Not asked in record or replay.
+     */
+    bool (*do_interrupt_unlocked)(CPUState *cpu);
     /** @cpu_exec_interrupt: Callback for processing interrupts in cpu_exec */
     bool (*cpu_exec_interrupt)(CPUState *cpu, int interrupt_request);
     /**
@@ -181,6 +187,14 @@
      * them. False when it cannot tell (a bit it does not know).
      */
     bool (*cpu_exec_interrupt_masked)(CPUState *cpu, int interrupt_request);
+    /**
+     * @cpu_exec_interrupt_unlocked: (optional) true if @cpu_exec_interrupt
+     * may take what @interrupt_request has (or find it masked) without the
+     * BQL: from the CPU's own state alone, a change of that state alone.
+     * Not asked for DEBUG, HALT or RESET (EXITTB is not in it), in record
+     * or replay, nor while single-stepping.
+     */
+    bool (*cpu_exec_interrupt_unlocked)(CPUState *cpu, int interrupt_request);
     /** @cpu_exec_reset: Callback for reset in cpu_exec.  */
     void (*cpu_exec_reset)(CPUState *cpu);
     /**
--- a/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c	2026-11-27 18:51:17.029798525 -0500
